{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.92,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "polarity",
      "components": ["Q1", "U6"],
      "pins": ["Q1.2", "Q1.3", "Q1.1", "U6.1", "U6.5", "U6.6"],
      "nets": ["+5V", "USBC_VBUS_IN", "Net-(Q1-G)"],
      "observed": "Q1's source (pin 2) is connected to +5V, its drain (pin 3) to USBC_VBUS_IN, and its gate to U6.GATE. U6.VIN is on USBC_VBUS_IN and U6.SENSE is on +5V.",
      "expected": "For the LTC4412 ideal-diode path, the P-channel MOSFET source should face the input supply and its drain the load/output, matching U6.VIN at the input and U6.SENSE at the output. Q1's source and drain are reversed in the netlist.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"+5V\") ... (node (ref \"Q1\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"S\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"USBC_VBUS_IN\") ... (node (ref \"Q1\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"D\")) ... (node (ref \"U6\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"VIN\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"Q1\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"G\")) (node (ref \"U6\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GATE\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"+5V\") ... (node (ref \"U6\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"SENSE\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "\"USB power-path controller intended to OR/protect a USB power input\""
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The reversed MOSFET orientation can prevent U6 from controlling the gate relative to the MOSFET source as intended, compromising the USB input power path and its reverse-current protection.",
      "confidence": 0.92
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The USB ideal-diode path has a P-channel MOSFET whose source and drain are opposite the expected LTC4412 input-to-output orientation. This can impair power-path operation and reverse-current blocking."
}

